Description: Module for gothi: ask a question, TINY answers in a speech bubble
 Adds the entry Ask the dolphin to the menu Modules of gothi (restart gothi after the installation): type a question on the keyboard (slide it out), press Enter and the dolphin answers in a speech bubble. The answers come from TINY, a neural network with 367,000 weights that knows about 3,500 facts (countries, animals, space, the body, simple sums, words); on other questions it can answer confidently and be wrong, and that is part of the fun.
 It only calls the command tiny of the package tiny in its plain text mode; the network runs on the phone, nothing is sent anywhere.
 Upstream: https://github.com/n900-resurrection/nokia-n900-apps
